            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for entry, then the Telugu for a pleasure trip."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: షికారు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "షికారు — ṣikāru — \"a jaunt; an outing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాయంత్రం మేము సముద్రం దగ్గర షికారుకు వెళ్ళాం. sāyantraṁ mēmu samudraṁ daggara ṣikāruku veḷḷāṁ. In the evening we went for a stroll by the sea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "షికారుకు వెళ్ళు, to go for an outing. An outing with no aim but pleasure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "షికారు (ṣikāru) is a loan from Persian shikār, \"hunting, the chase\", which reached Telugu through Hindustani; a hunting trip became any trip for pleasure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
