          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దృశ్యం — dṛśyaṁ — \"a view; a scene\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కొండ మీద నుంచి దృశ్యం చాలా అందంగా ఉంది. koṇḍa mīda nuñci dṛśyaṁ cālā andaṅgā undi. The view from the top of the hill is very beautiful."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A view of nature, and also a scene in a film or a play."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దృశ్యం (dṛśyaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit dṛśya, \"visible, what is to be seen\" (Monier-Williams), from dṛś, \"to see\"."
            }
