          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మజిలీ — majilī — \"a stopover; a halt\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రెండు రోజుల ప్రయాణంలో మొదటి మజిలీ ఒక చిన్న పట్టణం. reṇḍu rōjula prayāṇaṁlō modaṭi majilī oka cinna paṭṭaṇaṁ. On the two-day journey the first stopover was a small town."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A stop on a long journey. మజిలీ (majilī) కథలు are stories told at each halt of a journey."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మజిలీ (majilī) is usually traced to Arabic manzil, \"a place where travellers halt\", which came into Telugu through Persian and Hindustani."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
